// M18 Phase 1: a cell-based creature (research/m18-creature-biology.md).
// `kind: Creature` -- never moves via the CA sweep, exactly like `Plant`;
// relocated explicitly by the M18 active-site scheduler (`creature.rs`),
// which reads/writes it through the ordinary `World::get`/`set`.
//
// Flammable with real numbers, same treatment fire.rs already gives every
// other material kind uniformly -- this is the entire mechanism behind "a
// worm dies to fire", no creature-specific code needed for it at all.
// `ignition_temperature` is left unset (never spontaneously ignites from
// nearby heat alone): the worm's own thermotaxis (creature.rs) is what
// handles "near a fire" by fleeing before contact; only direct contact with
// a burning neighbour (flammability) should actually catch it alight,
// mirroring how a real animal that fails to flee in time gets burned.
// `density` doesn't drive movement for a Creature cell the way it does for
// a Powder (creature.rs never displaces via the CA sweep), but the field is
// still required and set to a plausible soft-tissue value.
(
    name: "worm",
    display: "Worm",
    kind: Creature,
    density: 1.0,
    colors: [
        (176, 92, 88),
        (166, 82, 78),
        (186, 102, 96),
    ],
    flammability: 0.6,
    burn_temperature: 500.0,
    burn_duration: 60,
    burns_into: "corpse",
    heat_conductivity: 0.1,
)
